      "id": 1,
      "text": "Chefornak was founded in the 1950s, so it lacks older architectural styles like Baroque or Classicism.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.kupi.com/en/explore/united-states/chefornak/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Tern Mountain, an extinct volcano about 387 feet high, towers south of Chefornak and reflects the area's volcanic past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/chefornak_alaska",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Chaputnguak School takes its name from Chaputnguak, Chefornak's original Yup'ik name meaning an object blocking a path.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chefornak%2C_Alaska",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Chefornak grew around a general store founded by Alexie Amagiqchik in the mid‑20th century, and it officially incorporated in 1974.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/chefornak_alaska",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Chefornak sits at the confluence of the Keggaluk and Kinia rivers, chosen for its high, flood‑protected ground.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.kupi.com/en/explore/united-states/chefornak/history",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Chefornak enjoys a subarctic marine climate, milder than interior Alaska yet highly variable because of the Bering Sea.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
